# Brother Tull and the dimming Lantern. Trust him, or poke at the story.
@id the_dimming
@title The Dimming
@trigger dusk_after crown_of_spoons
@order 60

== start
narrator: A monk in a lantern-orange robe waits politely at the counter until every customer is served.
tull (neutral): Forgive the intrusion. Brother Tull, keeper of the Great Lantern.
tull (sad): Look up. Do you see how it gutters? The Lantern dims a little more every season.
tull (neutral): The Hollow breathes sick air — from below the Cellars. The old Sunken Orchard.
tull (neutral): The guild will sell you a permit. It is expensive. Everything worth doing is.
* "If the town needs light, we'll go."
  ~ renown +5
  ~ affinity tull +1
  tull (happy): Then the Lantern has new friends. I will pray for full pantries.
* "That sounds like a sales pitch for permits."
  -> pitch
? flag find_rook -> rook
-> end

== pitch
tull (surprised): Ha! It does, doesn't it.
tull (sad): The truth is older and less flattering. The temple keeps records of what the Lantern burns.
tull (neutral): Come back when you've seen the Orchard. Then ask me about the tithe.
~ flag tithe_hint
? flag find_rook -> rook
-> end

== rook
tull (neutral): One more thing. You are looking for an old adventurer? A man with a scarred hand?
tull (happy): There is a tea stall two towns over, run by such a man. He hums when the tea is right.
pip (surprised): HE HUMS?! Maro hums!
-> end
